1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:01,144
Your chatbot answers.

2
00:00:01,576 --> 00:00:02,488
Why can't it act?

3
00:00:03,312 --> 00:00:04,517
If you are building AI

4
00:00:04,577 --> 00:00:06,968
projects, this difference decides what

5
00:00:06,988 --> 00:00:08,273
you actually build next.

6
00:00:08,974 --> 00:00:10,358
A chatbot is a software

7
00:00:10,398 --> 00:00:12,663
application that communicates with people

8
00:00:12,744 --> 00:00:14,067
through text or voice.

9
00:00:14,518 --> 00:00:15,482
Ask it when your exam

10
00:00:15,582 --> 00:00:17,370
is, and it answers, then

11
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:18,675
waits for your next message.

12
00:00:19,046 --> 00:00:20,929
An agent is different: a

13
00:00:21,009 --> 00:00:23,433
system that autonomously performs tasks

14
00:00:23,694 --> 00:00:25,617
by designing workflows with available

15
00:00:25,677 --> 00:00:26,038
tools.

16
00:00:26,408 --> 00:00:27,229
Give it a goal like

17
00:00:27,250 --> 00:00:29,313
"shortlist internships that match my

18
00:00:29,373 --> 00:00:31,016
résumé and add the deadlines

19
00:00:31,076 --> 00:00:32,679
to my calendar", and it

20
00:00:32,719 --> 00:00:35,223
plans the steps, searches, reads,

21
00:00:35,524 --> 00:00:37,287
shortlists and writes the entries

22
00:00:37,347 --> 00:00:37,728
itself.

23
00:00:38,118 --> 00:00:40,442
Anthropic describes agents as systems

24
00:00:40,822 --> 00:00:41,984
where the model directs its

25
00:00:42,104 --> 00:00:43,807
own process and tool use.

26
00:00:44,529 --> 00:00:45,628
So here is the test.

27
00:00:46,021 --> 00:00:47,251
If it only talks, it

28
00:00:47,292 --> 00:00:47,977
is a chatbot.

29
00:00:48,349 --> 00:00:49,272
If it pursues a goal

30
00:00:49,352 --> 00:00:50,657
and completes tasks for you,

31
00:00:51,119 --> 00:00:51,861
it is an agent.

32
